---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { strings } from '../../i18n/strings';
const t = strings.en;
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title={`Privacy Policy | ${t.brand}`} description="How we handle your data on nevnap.app — GDPR-compliant policy." altLangPath="/privacy">
  <article class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl pt-3 lg:pt-10">
    <nav class="nx-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol><li><a href="/en/">{t.brand}</a></li><li aria-hidden="true">›</li><li aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</li></ol>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="mt-6 nx-page-title nx-page-title--sm nx-rise">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-nx-subtle">Last updated: July 18, 2026.</p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-nx-muted leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">1. Data Controller</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Renátó Bogár (sole individual operator, hereinafter "Operator") informs users (hereinafter "You" / "User") about the data processing practices of the nevnap.app website and NévnapTárX mobile application.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:bogarrenato@gmail.com" class="text-nx-accent underline">bogarrenato@gmail.com</a></p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">2. What data do we collect?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">The website has no visitor registration and the Operator does not ask for a name, address or phone number to browse it. Hosting, analytics and advertising providers may nevertheless process technical data:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>IP address (processed by providers for connectivity and security)</li>
          <li>Browser type, version, operating system</li>
          <li>Pages visited, time spent</li>
          <li>Referrer page</li>
          <li>Device type (mobile/desktop)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">3. Purpose and legal basis</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Traffic analytics</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) — consent): service improvement.</li>
          <li><strong>Cookie management</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) — consent): via the cookie banner.</li>
          <li><strong>Ad serving</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) — consent): after AdSense approval and in line with Google's consent requirements for the EEA.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">4. Data Processors</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">We engage the following third-party processors:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (USA) — web hosting, CDN.</li>
          <li><strong>Google LLC</strong> (USA) — Google Analytics (anonymized).</li>
          <li><strong>Google Ireland Ltd.</strong> — Google AdSense code and consent-management services.</li>
          <li><strong>Apple Inc.</strong> and <strong>Google LLC</strong> — App Store, Google Play (mobile app only).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">5. Google advertising data</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">When ads are served, Google and its partners may place and read cookies and use web beacons, IP addresses or other technical identifiers. AdSense code is enabled only on edited publisher-content pages, not on programmatically generated name or date pages.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">See Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-nx-accent underline">How Google uses data from partner sites</a> notice. Personalised ads in the EEA will only be activated with a Google-certified consent management platform.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">6. Data retention</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>Analytics data: 14 months</li>
          <li>Cookie preferences: until changed or the browser's local storage is cleared</li>
          <li>Hosting and security logs: under Cloudflare's current retention rules</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">7. Your rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Under GDPR, every user has the right to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — what data we store</li>
          <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — correcting inaccurate data</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure</strong> ("right to be forgotten")</li>
          <li><strong>Restriction of processing</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Data portability</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Object</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">To exercise any right, email <a href="mailto:bogarrenato@gmail.com" class="text-nx-accent underline">bogarrenato@gmail.com</a>. We respond within <strong>30 days</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">8. Filing a complaint</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">You may file a complaint with the Hungarian Data Protection Authority (NAIH):</p>
        <address class="mt-2 not-italic">1055 Budapest, Falk Miksa utca 9-11. Hungary<br/><a href="https://www.naih.hu" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-nx-accent underline">www.naih.hu</a></address>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">9. Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">See our <a href="/en/cookies" class="text-nx-accent underline">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">10. Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">This policy may be updated. Significant changes are announced on the website. The update date is at the top.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
